        "original_id": "d68beb1c-2a59-5fdc-a21f-7fc03a2161ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnny Majors, Paul Hornung\n- Organizations: Tennessee Volunteers football team, Green Bay Packers, National Football League, Southeastern Conference\n- Places: Neyland Stadium, Knoxville, Tennessee\n- Roles: head coach, running back\n- Awards: Heisman Trophy, Pro Football Hall of Fame, Super Bowl\n\nFacts:\n- In 1956, Johnny Majors finished second to Paul Hornung in voting for the Heisman Trophy.\n- Paul Hornung was born on December 23, 1935.\n- Paul Hornung, nicknamed \"The Golden Boy,\" played as a professional American football player and Hall of Fame running back for the Green Bay Packers in the National Football League from 1957 to 1966.\n- Paul Hornung won four NFL titles and the first Super Bowl with the Green Bay Packers.\n- In 1990, the Tennessee Volunteers football team competed as a member of the Southeastern Conference.\n- In 1990, Johnny Majors served as the head coach of the Tennessee Volunteers football team in his 14th year.\n- In 1990, the Tennessee Volunteers football team played its home games at Neyland Stadium in Knoxville, Tennessee.",
